    "title": "Hearing set Jan. 8 on 5 MW solar farm planned on both sides of Holland Crossing Road - NewsBreak",
    "text": "5 hours ago\nBALTIMORE — The Maryland Public Service Commission (PSC) will hold a public hearing at the Crisfield Library on Thursday, Jan. 8 at 6:30 p.m. about plans for a 5 MW solar photovoltaic generating facility on both sides of Holland Crossing Road in Marion.\nThe hearing may be viewed online on the Public Utility Law Judge’s YouTube Channel, https://bit.ly/2X6wLiP . Written comments will be accepted until Monday, Jan. 12 either through the PSC’s Dropbox, which can be accessed at www.psc.md.us (instructions are available at www.psc.state.md.us/make-a-public-comment ) or by U.S. Mail to Jamie Bergin, Chief Clerk, Maryland Public Service Commission, William Donald Schaefer Tower, 6 St. Paul Street, 16th Floor, Baltimore MD 21202.\nAll comments must include a reference to Case No. 9783 (if regarding the SO19 Project) and/or 9784 (if regarding the SO201 Project). The applicants seeking a “Certificate of Public Convenience and Necessity” are TPE MD SO19 and TPE MD SO201 which are affiliated limited liability companies with document filings available on the PSC website.\nThe PSC, since the enactment of SB 931 during the 2025 General Assembly Session, is now the principal authority governing the approval of large-scale solar energy projects.",
